-- title:
--   Base change preserves kernels of degree d
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ and $B'$ be commutative rings in the same universe, with $B$ Noetherian, let $g \colon B \to B'$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $\varphi = (\varphi_0, \varphi_1)$ be a pair of formal power series in two variables over $B$ (an element of `Series B`, i.e. a family $\mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to B[[X_0,X_1]]$) with $\mathrm{constantCoeff}(\varphi_i) = 0$ for each $i$. Let $d$ be a natural number and assume `FormalODModule.HasKernelOfDegree φ d`, that is: writing $A_\varphi = B[[X_0,X_1]]/(\varphi_0,\varphi_1)$ for the quotient of the power series ring by the ideal generated by the range of $\varphi$, the $B$-module $A_\varphi$ is finite and projective, and for every field $\kappa$ in the ambient universe and every ring homomorphism $f \colon B \to \kappa$ the $\kappa$-vector space $\kappa[[X_0,X_1]]/(f_*\varphi_0, f_*\varphi_1)$ has dimension exactly $d$. The conclusion is that the same three conditions hold over $B'$ for the coefficientwise image $\varphi \cdot g = (g_*\varphi_0, g_*\varphi_1)$: `HasKernelOfDegree (φ.map g) d`.
--
--   This is the base-change statement for the kernel of a pair of power series without constant term, i.e. the assertion that a finite locally free kernel of degree $d$ stays finite locally free of the same degree after an arbitrary change of base ring $B \to B'$, with $B$ Noetherian. It is the form in which finiteness and degree data are transported along base change throughout the work with formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules — for instance for the multiplication-by-$p$ series and for rigidifying isogenies — and it is invoked by the composition and divisibility lemmas for `HasKernelOfDegree` and by the base-change statements for critical charts.
